{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/013-final-review-amendment-fixes-ts-rev-001-003-004/20260315090201-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nartifact: spec\nloop: 13\nproject: tank-sim\nbackend: claude(opus)\nrole: planner\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T09:02:01Z\n---\n\n4 of 5 final review amendments remain unimplemented. I'll write a spec to address them.\n\n# Feature: Final Review Amendment Fixes (TS-REV-001, 003, 004, 005)\n\n## Description\nImplement the four outstanding final review amendments identified during the Loop 12 completion review. TS-REV-002 (alkalinity double-charge) is already correctly implemented via the budget mechanism. The remaining four amendments fix: (1) early validation of water-change source profiles, (2) removal of spurious DIC-driven alkalinity drift, (3) filter cleanliness decay during normal play, and (4) dissolved oxygen mixing during water changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] **TS-REV-001** — `apply_action` rejects `WaterChangePercent` with an unknown `source_profile_id` immediately, returning a `SimError` before the action is enqueued. The step-time validation in `water_change.rs` is kept as a defensive fallback but is no longer the primary gate.\n- [ ] **TS-REV-003** — `step_hourly_chemistry` in `chemistry.rs` no longer modifies `alkalinity_meq_total`. pH is recomputed from the existing alkalinity and updated DIC only. Nitrification and water changes remain the sole alkalinity drivers.\n- [ ] **TS-REV-004** — `cleanliness_index` decays daily proportional to detritus load and bioload. A moderately stocked, unfed tank should see negligible decay; an overfed tank should see measurable decay within 2–4 weeks. `CleanFilter` restores `cleanliness_index` proportionally to its `intensity` parameter. The `update_daily_filter_clogging` formula is corrected so that clogging can actually accumulate during normal simulation.\n- [ ] **TS-REV-005** — `apply_water_change` exchanges `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` using the same retention/replacement pattern as other dissolved pools. Replacement oxygen is derived from saturation at the source water temperature (reusing existing DO saturation logic).\n- [ ] All existing acceptance tests still pass (determinism, save/load, mass balance, tank size response, etc.).\n- [ ] A new integration test `water_change_do_mixing` confirms that after a 50% water change, DO total is within 1% of the expected mixed value.\n- [ ] A new integration test `filter_cleanliness_decay` confirms that after 30 days of moderate feeding with no cleaning, `cleanliness_index` is measurably below 1.0.\n- [ ] A new unit test `apply_action_rejects_bad_source_profile` confirms that `apply_action(WaterChangePercent { source_profile_id: \"nonexistent\", .. })` returns `Err(SimError::...)` without enqueueing.\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — Add source-profile validation inside `apply_action` for `WaterChangePercent` actions; keep `CleanFilter` handler consistent with revised cleanliness model\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` — Remove the `ALKALINITY_FEEDBACK_MEQ_PER_MG_C` term and any line that mutates `alkalinity_meq_total` based on DIC delta\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` — Rewrite `update_daily_filter_clogging` so that `cleanliness_index` decays from detritus pressure; the clogging formula should use `cleanliness_index` directly (not `1.0 - cleanliness_index` in a way that zeroes out when clean)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs` — Add `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` to the remove/replace cycle; derive source-water DO from saturation at source temperature\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` — Clarify `cleanliness_index` docs if needed; no structural change expected\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/` — Add `water_change_do_mixing`, `filter_cleanliness_decay`, and `apply_action_rejects_bad_source_profile` tests\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Loop 11 (Substrate Effect Wiring and Filter Causal Integration) — already completed\n- Blocks: Project completion sign-off\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
